tion - Augmentation rather than replacement\",\n      \"Ethical Challenges - Privacy, bias, and regulatory concerns\"\n    ],\n    \"importantQuotes\": [\n      {\n        \"text\": \"AI-powered imaging analysis can now detect certain cancers earlier than human radiologists.\",\n        \"context\": \"Opening statement of Diagnostic Revolution section, establishing AI's superior capabilities\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"What might take a radiologist 15 minutes to analyze, an AI system can process in seconds, allowing radiologists to focus on complex cases and treatment planning rather than routine image analysis.\",\n        \"context\": \"Explaining the efficiency advantage of AI in diagnostic workflows\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"AI enables truly personalized medicine by analyzing a patient's genetic data, medical history, lifestyle factors, and molecular markers.\",\n        \"context\": \"Defining the comprehensive data analysis behind personalized medicine\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"Rather than replacing doctors, AI will augment medical professionals by handling routine diagnostic tasks, flagging unusual cases for specialist review, suggesting treatment options based on latest research, and monitoring patient outcomes to improve care.\",\n        \"context\": \"Vision of collaborative human-AI healthcare future in The Path Forward section\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"ideas\": {\n    \"hooks\": [\n      {\n        \"text\": \"The day a machine saw my mother's cancer before her doctor did changed how I think about medicine forever.\",\n        \"type\": \"emotional\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"What if the secret to curing cancer isn't in a lab, but in lines of code running on servers?\",\n        \"type\": \"curiosity\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"AI isn't making medicine better - it's creating a healthcare system where machines make life-or-death decisions without human oversight.\",\n        \"type\": \"controversy\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"A single AI system can analyze 10,000 medical images in the time it takes a radiologist to review one - and with 95% accuracy in cancer detection.\",\n        \"type\": \"statistic\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"text\": \"When Dr. Chen first saw the AI's diagnosis, she dismissed it as a computer error. Six months later, the biopsy proved the machine was right.\",\n        \"type\": \"story\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"angles\": [\n      {\n        \"perspective\": \"The Patient's Dilemma\",\n        \"approach\": \"Explore the tension between faster, more accurate diagnoses and loss of human connection in medicine through patient stories and ethical considerations.\",\n        \"target\": \"General readers concerned about depersonalization of healthcare\",\n        \"relevanceScore\": 0.8\n      },\n      {\n        \"perspective\": \"The Overworked Doctor's Relief\",\n        \"approach\": \"Focus on how AI alleviates burnout among medical professionals by handling routine tasks, featuring interviews with radiologists and surgeons.\",\n        \"target\": \"Healthcare professionals and medical students\",\n        \"relevanceScore\": 0.9\n      },\n      {\n        \"perspective\": \"The Algorithm's Blind Spots\",\n        \"approach\": \"Investigate cases where AI diagnostic tools failed due to biased training data, examining the real-world consequences for minority patients.\",\n        \"target\": \"Tech ethicists, policymakers, and social justice advocates\",\n        \"relevanceScore\": 0.7\n      },\n      {\n        \"perspective\": \"The Startup Disruptor\",\n        \"approach\": \"Profile AI healthcare startups racing to commercialize diagnostic tools, analyzing the billion-dollar market and regulatory hurdles.\",\n        \"target\": \"Investors, entrepreneurs, and business readers\",\n        \"relevanceScore\": 0.6\n      },\n      {\n        \"perspective\": \"The Global Health Equalizer\",\